ublished_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If your life total is brought to 0 or less at the same time that Stuffy Doll is dealt damage, you lose the game before its triggered ability goes on the stack.","oracle_id":"499dceab-1890-49c8-b35d-b059a1dc950f","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
